From 091cb8c7f99b0b796af50f19288f78a83dadfe96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:06:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] fix: apply the image's environment, and check the
 no-runtime path in CI

A container runtime hands a process the environment the image declares, and
nothing of its own. Both halves matter here: JULIA_DEPOT_PATH points Julia at
the image's precompiled Oscar depot and SAGE_BIN names the Sage build, while an
inherited PYTHONPATH, LD_LIBRARY_PATH or XDG_CONFIG_HOME would shadow the
image's own modules and paths. docker/sage-image.py read the config but ran
with a fixed minimal environment on top of the caller's; it now clears the
caller's environment, applies the config's Env recorded in the cache stamp,
sets HOME and TMPDIR, and lets --env override one entry.

The bubblewrap preflight named /proc/sys/kernel/unprivileged_userns_clone but
not the AppArmor restriction Ubuntu 24.04 and later apply. There the packaged
bwrap-userns-restrict profile permits bubblewrap -- this host has the
restriction switched on and works because of that profile -- and a host
without the profile needs kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0. The
diagnostic and SAGE-ENVIRONMENT.md now name whichever piece is missing.

research-environment-image.yml gains a job that fetches the published image
and runs its own check with no container runtime in use, so the path a host
without Docker, chroot or PRoot depends on is exercised after every publish.

Verified on this host, which uses no Docker, no chroot and no PRoot: `run`
executes the image's Sage and its partn_ref canonical label, mounts a consumer
checkout at /work, reproduces the published image's bliss segfault, and exposes
only the image's environment; `check` runs the image's research environment
check to completion and reports SageMath 11.0.beta5 with its Julia/Oscar bridge
and every Lean toolchain (exit 0); `apply_layer` removes a whited-out file,
clears an opaque directory and preserves a symlink on synthetic layers;
`resolve` returns the config digest and all 18 layer digests of the image that
was unpacked independently. Not verified: the new CI job (not run here), a
complete 13.6 GB `fetch` (manifest and layer digests resolve, the first layers
download and verify, but the registry slowed below 100 kB/s inside layer 7),
and a host whose kernel refuses user namespaces outright.
